Z||000000||MooCow||10-13-2000||06:30 PM||||Is this thisa good trade or not??<BR>I know that Ed Parks wouldn't srew me or anyone over but still.  I'm driving all the way from Michigan to Alabam the first weekend in November.  The trade it My 86 SE V6 4-speed stick for the same year and color and power everything like mine but his is an Auto which I really want.  His has clost to 100K and mine has 132K.  I will be giving him my car and about 3-4 hundred dollars. <BR>Sound like a good deal or not.<P>                             Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||10-13-2000||06:36 PM||||Well,it really depends on the shape of the car. <BR>Exterior, does it have any damage or need paint. <BR>Interior, is the dash cracked,seats stained or torn, door panels in good condition.<P>The thing is that you're trading a car that you've owned for awhile, so you know it's "personality"<BR>The new car is just that, it's history is unknown to you, you don't know what someone else has done to it. <BR>For instance, I bought my 85Gt and later found that the previous owner had cut about a foot of wire from the harness going to the speedometer sensor.<BR>But as far as the Financial end is concerned it sounds pretty cool <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Good Luck!!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
